Gravity UI (uikit) is set up. I'll implement a button that opens a modal (Dialog or Modal from @gravity-ui/uikit) with text and confirm/cancel actions.

Gravity UI has `Modal`, `Dialog`, `Button`, `Text` components. I'll use `Dialog` with `Dialog.Footer` for confirm/cancel buttons, or a Modal with custom content. The Dialog component with onButtonClickCancel/onButtonClickApply is the canonical pattern.

Let me write App.tsx:

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { Button, Dialog, Text } from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

export function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);

  return (
    <div style={{ padding: 24 }}>
      <Button view="action" size="l" onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>
        Открыть модальное окно
      </Button>
      <Dialog
        open={open}
        onClose={() => setOpen(false)}
        onButtonClickApply={() => setOpen(false)}
        onButtonClickCancel={() => setOpen(false)}
        textButtonApply="Подтвердить"
        textButtonCancel="Отмена"
        size="s"
      >
        <Dialog.Header caption="Подтверждение" />
        <Dialog.Body>
          <Text>Вы уверены, что хотите выполнить это действие?</Text>
        </Dialog.Body>
        <Dialog.Footer
          onClickButtonApply={() => setOpen(false)}
          onClickButtonCancel={() => setOpen(false)}
          textButtonApply="Подтвердить"
          textButtonCancel="Отмена"
        />
      </Dialog>
    </div>
  );
}
```

In Gravity UI, Dialog.Footer takes props: onClickButtonCancel, onClickButtonApply, textButtonCancel, textButtonApply. Dialog has onClose, onOpenChange. Actually the Dialog props: `open`, `onClose` (or onOpenChange). Dialog.Footer handles the buttons. There are no onButtonClickApply props on Dialog directly — those belong to Dialog.Footer.

Maybe show a result feedback, e.g., display "Подтверждено" text after confirming? Nice touch but keep it simple. The user asked in Russian, so UI text in Russian.

